{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1019","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1019","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1019\",\"parent_revision\":\"e9ea9d1d10ef99ebd3a4e0035f58d8e1a46fc147da35a2d09a9a3b3e56154100\",\"root_revision\":\"e9ea9d1d10ef99ebd3a4e0035f58d8e1a46fc147da35a2d09a9a3b3e56154100\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe groom-milestone skill produces a dispatch plan (conflict groups, wave assignments, quality gates) but the orchestrator has no MCP tool to persist it. Four dispatch execution tools exist (dispatch_wave_start, dispatch_item_status, dispatch_wave_status, dispatch_spawn) but no dispatch plan creation tool. The write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path) Python function exists in dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py \u2014 it needs an MCP wrapper in backlog_core/dispatch.py so the orchestrator can persist plans without calling Python functions or writing YAML directly.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Add dispatch_create_plan MCP tool\\nGoal: Add MCP tool wrapping write_dispatch_plan() for orchestrator-driven dispatch plan persistence\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. write_dispatch_plan function signature | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: yaml_writer.py:63 confirmed by fact-checker\\n2. DispatchPlan model structure | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: groomer quoted model fields from models.py\\n3. Existing dispatch MCP tool patterns | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker confirmed 4 tools in backlog_core/server.py using @mcp.tool, async, Annotated params\\n4. FastMCP v3 patterns | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker confirmed FastMCP v3 (@mcp.tool without parens, task=True for background)\\n5. groom-milestone SKILL.md Step 9 | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst confirmed needs update\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Conditions 2, 3, 4: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker and groomer agents)\\n- File location correction: dispatch tools are in backlog_core/server.py, not backlog_core/dispatch.py\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 all 5 conditions AVAILABLE, no MISSING inputs\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add dispatch_create_plan mcp tool for orchestrator-driven dispatch plan persistence** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Grooming investigation of #1013, confirmed by dispatch-tools-researcher agent (2026-03-22)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-22)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nThe `/groom-milestone` skill produces a dispatch plan (DispatchPlan model) containing conflict groups, wave assignments, and quality gates. This plan must be persisted to a YAML file (e.g., `plan/milestone-3-dispatch.yaml`) to be read by `/work-milestone` for execution. The four existing dispatch tools handle execution (`dispatch_wave_start`, `dispatch_item_status`, `dispatch_wave_status`, `dispatch_spawn`), but there is no MCP tool to persist the plan itself.\\n\\n**Current workaround**: Agents must call `write_dispatch_plan()` directly as a Python function inside a delegation. This bypasses the MCP interface and requires agents to import from `dispatch_schema.writers.yaml_writer` \u2014 a tight coupling that violates the tool-driven architecture.\\n\\n**Gap**: Orchestrators cannot use MCP to persist dispatch plans. The tool must be added to `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` and registered with FastMCP v3.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n**DispatchPlan model** (dispatch_schema/core/models.py:117-128):\\n```python\\nclass DispatchPlan(_DispatchBase):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Root model for plan/milestone-{N}-dispatch.yaml.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    milestone: MilestoneHeader\\n    conflict_groups: list[ConflictGroup] = Field(\\n        default_factory=list, validation_alias=AliasChoices(\\\"conflict_groups\\\", \\\"conflict-groups\\\")\\n    )\\n    waves: list[Wave] = Field(..., min_length=1)\\n    quality_gates: QualityGates = Field(\\n        default_factory=QualityGates, validation_alias=AliasChoices(\\\"quality_gates\\\", \\\"quality-gates\\\")\\n    )\\n```\\n\\n**write_dispatch_plan signature** (dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py:63-115):\\n```python\\ndef write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path) -> Path:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Write a dispatch plan to YAML using atomic rename.\\n    \\n    Serializes the plan with kebab-case keys. Writes to a temp file in the\\n    same directory as ``path``, then renames atomically to prevent partial\\n    writes on crash. Creates parent directories if they do not exist.\\n    ...\\n    Raises:\\n        ValueError: If ``path`` resolves to a symlink.\\n        OSError: If the write or rename fails.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n```\\n\\n**Existing dispatch tool pattern** (test_dispatch_tools.py:157-179):\\n- Tool calls return dict[str, Any]\\n- Success responses include: milestone, status, items_count, messages, warnings\\n- Error responses include: error key (string)\\n- All tools use FastMCP @mcp.tool() decorator\\n- Response dict contract enforced in test assertions\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nAgents planning dispatch workflows must work around the missing tool by:\\n1. Calling Python functions directly instead of MCP tools\\n2. Importing from dispatch_schema (tight coupling)\\n3. Handling file I/O themselves instead of delegating to the MCP server\\n\\nThis violates the stateless-handoff principle where all state changes go through MCP tools. Once the tool is available, dispatch planning will be fully accessible to orchestrators and agents via MCP.\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\nOne new MCP tool: `dispatch_create_plan(plan_json: str, path: str) -> dict`\\n\\n**Input:**\\n- `plan_json` \u2014 JSON string representation of a DispatchPlan model (passed as JSON, not YAML, since MCP doesn't handle structured object parameters directly)\\n- `path` \u2014 target file path relative to repo root (e.g., `plan/milestone-3-dispatch.yaml`)\\n\\n**Processing:**\\n- Parse plan_json into a DispatchPlan Pydantic model (validates all required fields)\\n- Call `write_dispatch_plan(plan, Path(path))` from dispatch_schema.writers.yaml_writer\\n- Return dict with: `{\\\"path\\\": str, \\\"status\\\": \\\"created\\\"|\\\"updated\\\", \\\"messages\\\": list, \\\"warnings\\\": list}` or `{\\\"error\\\": str}`\\n\\n**Follows established patterns:**\\n- `@mcp.tool()` decorator (non-task tool, not background)\\n- Parameter types: str for JSON, str for path\\n- Return type: dict with error key on failure, optional messages/warnings lists\\n- No symlink traversal (write_dispatch_plan already validates this)\\n- Parent directory creation handled by write_dispatch_plan (atomic rename)\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Create or modify:**\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 add dispatch_create_plan tool definition + registration\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` \u2014 add TestDispatchCreatePlan class with 4-5 test cases:\\n   - Happy path: valid DispatchPlan JSON creates file\\n   - Error path: invalid JSON fails gracefully\\n   - Symlink rejection: path is a symlink, returns error\\n   - Path creation: parent directories created automatically\\n   - File overwrite: existing file is updated atomically\\n\\n**Reference (read-only):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 DispatchPlan, MilestoneHeader, Wave, ConflictGroup, WaveItem, QualityGates\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py` \u2014 write_dispatch_plan, _keys_to_kebab, _make_yaml\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- `dispatch_schema` package \u2014 already exists, provides DispatchPlan model and write_dispatch_plan function\\n- FastMCP v3 server \u2014 already running (backlog_core/server.py)\\n- Pydantic \u2014 already required by dispatch_schema for model validation\\n- ruamel.yaml \u2014 already required by dispatch_schema.writers.yaml_writer\\n\\nNo new external dependencies needed.\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\nAPPROVED \u2014 straightforward MCP tool addition following established dispatch tool patterns. The function already exists, is tested, handles atomicity and security. The MCP wrapper is a thin adapter layer that deserializes JSON, validates via Pydantic, calls write_dispatch_plan, and returns a dict response. Implementation complexity is minimal (~20 lines). Test coverage mirrors the existing dispatch_wave_start, dispatch_item_status pattern.\\n\\n## Code Producers\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Files that will be created or modified:**\\n\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (MODIFY)\\n   - Add `dispatch_create_plan()` MCP tool function (~20-30 lines)\\n   - Follows @mcp.tool decorator pattern used by dispatch_wave_start, dispatch_item_status, dispatch_wave_status\\n   - Input: plan_json (str), path (str)\\n   - Output: dict with path, status, messages, warnings keys (or error key)\\n   - Calls write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path) from dispatch_schema.writers.yaml_writer\\n\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` (MODIFY)\\n   - Add TestDispatchCreatePlan test class with 4-5 test cases:\\n     * test_dispatch_create_plan_happy_path \u2014 valid DispatchPlan JSON creates file\\n     * test_dispatch_create_plan_invalid_json \u2014 malformed JSON returns error gracefully\\n     * test_dispatch_create_plan_parent_dirs \u2014 parent directories created automatically\\n     * test_dispatch_create_plan_file_overwrite \u2014 existing file updated atomically\\n   - Follows existing test pattern from TestDispatchWaveStart (lines 157-179)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Code Consumers Current Users Of Dispatch Tools\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Files that will potentially reference dispatch_create_plan in the future:**\\n\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md` (REFERENCE)\\n   - Step 9 (\\\"Persist plan to disk\\\") may be updated post-implementation to mention dispatch_create_plan MCP tool as alternative to Python function calls\\n   - Currently documents the gap; Step 9 likely calls write_dispatch_plan directly\\n\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` (REFERENCE)\\n   - Documents dispatch tools inventory\\n   - Section on \\\"Dispatch Orchestration System\\\" lists dispatch_wave_start, dispatch_item_status, dispatch_wave_status, dispatch_spawn\\n   - Will need entry for dispatch_create_plan when added\\n\\n3. `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` (REFERENCE)\\n   - Reads dispatch plans produced by groom-milestone\\n   - May reference dispatch_create_plan as the tool that persists those plans\\n   - Shows usage flow: groom-milestone (creates plan via MCP) \u2192 work-milestone (reads plan)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Documentation\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Files that document dispatch system:**\\n\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` (UPDATE)\\n   - Section: \\\"Dispatch Orchestration System\\\"\\n   - Current inventory: dispatch_wave_start, dispatch_item_status, dispatch_wave_status, dispatch_spawn\\n   - Will add: dispatch_create_plan to complete the tool set\\n\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/references/dispatch-plan-schema.md` (REFERENCE)\\n   - Documents DispatchPlan model structure\\n   - Consumed by both groom-milestone (producer) and work-milestone (consumer)\\n   - No changes needed; schema remains stable\\n\\n3. `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` (REFERENCE)\\n   - Section: \\\"Dispatch Orchestration System\\\" lists MCP tools\\n   - Lists: dispatch_wave_start, dispatch_item_status, dispatch_wave_status, dispatch_spawn\\n   - Will add: dispatch_create_plan tool description\\n</div>\\n\\n## Agent Instructions\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Files with agent-facing dispatch documentation:**\\n\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` (NO CHANGE)\\n   - Task-worker executes individual tasks, not responsible for plan creation\\n   - Dispatch orchestration is orchestrator-level concern\\n\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md` (REFERENCE)\\n   - Groom-milestone agent produces DispatchPlan\\n   - Currently documents workaround (call write_dispatch_plan directly)\\n   - Post-implementation: Step 9 can reference dispatch_create_plan MCP tool as the proper pattern\\n   - Agent instructions may emphasize stateless-handoff principle (all state changes via MCP)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Affected subsystems:**\\n\\n1. **Dispatch Schema System** (no changes)\\n   - `dispatch_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 DispatchPlan, Wave, WaveItem, ConflictGroup, MilestoneHeader, QualityGates models\\n   - `dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py` \u2014 write_dispatch_plan() function\\n   - Tests: `tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_yaml_writer.py`\\n   - Stable; new tool is a thin wrapper\\n\\n2. **MCP Server (backlog_core)** (1 tool added)\\n   - `backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 FastMCP v3 server definition\\n   - New tool: dispatch_create_plan\\n   - Follows existing dispatch tool patterns\\n\\n3. **Dispatch Execution State System** (no changes)\\n   - `backlog_core/dispatch_state.py` \u2014 SQLite state manager (used by dispatch_spawn)\\n   - Unaffected by dispatch plan creation tool\\n   - Plan creation is stateless (file write only)\\n\\n4. **Test Suite** (1 test class added)\\n   - `tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` \u2014 dispatch tool integration tests\\n   - New test class: TestDispatchCreatePlan\\n   - Validates dispatch_create_plan MCP tool behavior\\n</div>\\n\\n## Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] **MCP Tool Signature Correct**: dispatch_create_plan(plan_json: str, path: str) -> dict with @mcp.tool() decorator\\n- [ ] **Error Handling**: Returns {error: str} on validation failure, symlink rejection, or write failure\\n- [ ] **Pydantic Validation**: Deserializes JSON string to DispatchPlan model (validates all required fields)\\n- [ ] **Atomicity**: Delegates to write_dispatch_plan() which uses tempfile + atomic rename\\n- [ ] **Parent Directories**: write_dispatch_plan() handles directory creation\\n- [ ] **Test Coverage**: 4-5 test cases covering happy path, invalid JSON, file overwrite, directory creation\\n- [ ] **Documentation Updated**: ARCHITECTURE.md and CLAUDE.md updated to list dispatch_create_plan\\n- [ ] **groom-milestone Step 9**: May reference new tool as pattern (optional post-implementation improvement)\\n- [ ] **No New Dependencies**: Uses existing Pydantic, FastMCP, ruamel.yaml, dispatch_schema\\n- [ ] **Backwards Compatible**: Existing dispatch tools unchanged; only additive change\\n</div>\\n\\n## Claims Verified\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAll 5 claims VERIFIED with source evidence.\\n\\n### Claim 1: Four dispatch execution MCP tools exist\\n**VERIFIED** \u2713\\n- `dispatch_wave_start` \u2014 backlog_core/server.py:2055\\n- `dispatch_item_status` \u2014 backlog_core/server.py:2101\\n- `dispatch_wave_status` \u2014 backlog_core/server.py:2161\\n- `dispatch_spawn` \u2014 backlog_core/server.py:2407 (with task=True flag for background execution)\\n\\n### Claim 2: No dispatch plan creation MCP tool exists\\n**VERIFIED** \u2713\\n- Full grep of @mcp.tool definitions in server.py finds 37 tools total\\n- None are named dispatch_create_plan, dispatch_plan_create, or similar\\n- All dispatch_* tools are execution/status tools, not creation tools\\n\\n### Claim 3: write_dispatch_plan() exists in dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py\\n**VERIFIED** \u2713\\n- Location: dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py:63\\n- Signature: `def write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path) -> Path:`\\n- Implementation uses atomic rename (tempfile + os.rename) for crash-safe writes\\n- Returns the path written to\\n\\n### Claim 4: Dispatch tools are in backlog_core/server.py\\n**VERIFIED** \u2713\\n- Full path: /home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py\\n- All 4 dispatch_* tools defined in this file\\n\\n### Claim 5: Tools use FastMCP v3 patterns\\n**VERIFIED** \u2713\\n- Import statement: `from fastmcp import Context, FastMCP` (line 22)\\n- Server init: `mcp = FastMCP(\\\"backlog\\\", instructions=..., version=\\\"0.1.0\\\")` (lines 80-88)\\n- Decorator pattern: `@mcp.tool` (no parentheses) \u2014 v3 standard\\n- Function patterns: async functions with Annotated[type, Field(...)] from pydantic\\n- Dispatch spawn uses `@mcp.tool(task=True)` for background task pattern (v3)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-dispatch-create-plan-mcp-tool.md | current | feature-researcher | 2026-03-22T20:22:58.129591+00:00 |\\n| codebase-analysis | plan/codebase/dispatch-mcp-tool-patterns.md | current | codebase-analyzer | 2026-03-22T20:23:09.529949+00:00 |\\n| architect | plan/architect-dispatch-create-plan-mcp-tool.md | current | python-cli-design-spec | 2026-03-22T20:26:32.203168+00:00 |\\n| task-plan | plan/P1019-dispatch-create-plan-mcp-tool.yaml 